    {
      "id": "claim_202ceb851c9849ecb1b23cb4033b984e",
      "statement": "polyfill.js applies three patch mechanisms for the Hermes/Uint8Array gaps that @solana/web3.js, @solana/kit, Anchor, and Meteora DLMM hit: Buffer.prototype.subarray/slice are wrapped to restore Buffer prototypes via Object.setPrototypeOf (fixing Anchor discriminator extraction), ~27 Buffer read/write/copy/fill methods are injected onto Uint8Array.prototype forwarding through a zero-copy Buffer view (fixing buffer-layout deserialization), and Uint8Array.prototype.equals is implemented directly for Anchor discriminator comparisons.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L165-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b63a0015dc8ab10f2f05d8dbfb018055e29cd0a859ecb2b06c2cd5b7a8b7746:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://polyfill.js#L12-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c42964010db6d304b6274ca281d8b0ba8275724ace57d1cd3b5a967dba28328:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://polyfill.js#L36-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00e44df179f0ea1316d0ebe133aa646fd2d8b5dd3b69a119c838ac3cac8d6a01:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3a10790bf6cd4ee69b640e86a5642c90",
      "statement": "When a Solana SDK throws 'X is not a function' for a Buffer method, the required fix is to extend polyfill.js (add to the forwarding list or use the setPrototypeOf pattern); forking the SDK, swapping @craftzdog/react-native-buffer for the npm buffer package, or changing the polyfill load order are all prohibited. On web Metro resolves polyfill.web.js instead, which only sets global.Buffer from the npm buffer package since browsers already provide crypto and URL.",
      "evidence": [
