      "statement": "Native-only integrations hide behind five platform-split module pairs that Metro resolves by platform extension (the .web sibling loads only on web, native never sees it): polyfill(.web).js, src/wallet/walletKit(.web).tsx, src/hooks/useWidgetSync(.web).ts, src/widgets/registerWidgetTask(.web).ts, and src/observe/index(.web).tsx. App code imports only the native-named module; each pair's exports must be edited together or exactly one platform breaks. The web wallet stub renders children inertly with a throwing signIn, and the web Observe stub exports no-ops importing only ObserveConfig as a type so the native package never loads on web.",
